1. `If we asked year , months , days ` : then we can code like , provided year is given as 365 , number 
    of days in month as 30 days . 
    int n;
    cin >> n;
    int year = 0;
    int month = 0;
    int days = 0;
    year = n/365;
    n = n%365;
    month = n/30;
    n = n%30;
    days = n;
    days = n;
    cout << year << " years" << '\n';
    cout << month << " months" << '\n';
    cout << days<< " days" << '\n';
    
    
2. `Two find last two digits of a number ` : `n%100` this will give last two digits and want 3 then `n%1000` we 
    can find n numbers using this modulo trick , provided our number consist of atleast n digits. 
    
    
3. `If asked find last two digits after multiply four variables` : obviously this will exceed even long long variable
    and to get this i can do below approach . Logic behind this is that last two digits will decide the last two digits
    only and doing modulo with 100 this will shortern our number . 
    	 
	 int a, b, c,d;
    cin >> a >> b >> c >> d;
    a %= 100;
    b %= 100;
    c %= 100;
    d %= 100;

    int ans = a*b*c*d;
    int l_t_d = ans %100;
    if(l_t_d <= 9){
        cout << 0 << l_t_d << '\n';
    }
    else {
        cout <<  l_t_d << '\n';

    }
    
    
4. `When we don't know the number of inputs in competitive programming` : In such types of conditions we have to
    loop over the inputs until our condition for terminating the program doesn't matches . 
	1. `Ex` : In below example we terminated our program as it matches to 1999 as password.
	```cpp
	int x;
  while(cin >> x){
    if(x == 1999){
        cout << "Correct" << '\n';
        return;
    } 
    else{
        cout << "Wrong" << '\n';
    }
  }
	```
	
	
5. `To add any char or substring backside of a string ` :
	1. `First way` : `s += a;` if a is a variable of char or string type in which either we initialized or 
	    usually taken input from user.
	2. `Second way` : `s.push_back(a);` if a is a variable of char type this pushback method only accepts 
	    a single char and to send a substring to back use method 1.
	3. `Third way` : `s.push_back('a');`  to add a as a  character at end of string and this  pushback only
	    takes character and not substring . 
	    
    
6. `whenever you wanted to print something using function then use void function` :
        void sum(int a, int b){
        int sum = a+b;
       cout << sum << '\n';
    }

    void solve()
    {
        int x,y;
        cin >> x >> y;
        sum(x,y);
       
    }
    
    
7. `floor` : Is a mathematical function that takes a real number X and its output is the greatest integer less than or equal to X .


8. `ceil` : Is a mathematical function that takes a real number X and its output is the smallest integer larger than or equal to X.


9. `round` :  Is a mathematical function that takes a real number X and its output is the closest integer to that number X.


10. `swap()` : very very powerful function when you wanted to swap any two same data types , map or any complex structure but
    all things are same means if you are swapping 2 data types then they should of same type , if using map then all credential
    means key-value pair should be of same type . then `swap(a,b);` now b will become a and a will become b. 
    
    
11. `gcd(a,b);` use this to calculate greatest common divisor of two non zero numbers a and b. And this comes under numeric header. 
